Each process opens its own VF with vollo_rt_add_device and loads that VF's virtual program with vollo_rt_load_program, in place of the usual vollo_rt_add_accelerator and .vollo program: vollo_rt_context_t ctx;
EXIT_ON_ERROR(vollo_rt_init(&ctx));
EXIT_ON_ERROR(vollo_rt_add_device(ctx, 0, "0.3"));
EXIT_ON_ERROR(vollo_rt_load_program(ctx, "virtual-programs/vf-003.vollo-vf")); Here, the 0 is the accelerator's index within this context, and "0.3" is the VF to open. VF 0.3 must load vf-003.vollo-vf. When a process loads a virtual program, the runtime checks that the file matches the current deployment, so always use the files from the latest setup-vfs. After that, you use vollo-rt exactly as you would with a single accelerator. See the C API .

